Kernir patch 0013: freeing a write handle without close ends the gzip, xz and zip compressors

Upstream: libarchive 3.8.10, libarchive/archive_write_add_filter_gzip.c (free_data),
libarchive/archive_write_add_filter_xz.c (free_data) and libarchive/archive_write_set_format_zip.c (struct zip,
archive_write_zip_header, archive_write_zip_finish_entry, archive_write_zip_free). Applies on top of 0012.

archive_write_free skips close on a handle in state FATAL, which is how Kernir frees an unfinished write
(archive_write_fail first: close would pad the open entry with zeros up to its declared size, Int64.max bytes
for a crafted header, and 7z pads into its temporary file where no write error can stop it). Upstream ends
the gzip filter's deflate stream, the xz filter's lzma stream and the zip writer's per-entry deflate, bzip2,
lzma/xz or zstd stream only in close, so every cancelled or failed save kept that state: 256 KiB for gzip and
zip deflate, 93 MiB for xz at the default level, 673 MiB at level 9. The bzip2 filter and the 7zip writer
already end theirs in free.

The gzip and xz filters' free_data now call deflateEnd and lzma_end: both are no-ops on a stream that close
ended or open never started (the filter data is calloc'd). The zip writer records whether the entry's
compressor is live (set when write_header started it, cleared when finish_entry ended it) and ends a live one
in free and at the start of the next write_header, while entry_compression still names it. finish_entry's
error paths that end the stream themselves leave the flag set; their end calls are no-ops when repeated, and
the zstd context is set to NULL once freed. Successful archives are byte-identical.

Apply from Sources/CLibArchive: patch -p1 < patches/0013-write-free-ends-compressors.patch

--- a/libarchive/archive_write_add_filter_gzip.c
+++ b/libarchive/archive_write_add_filter_gzip.c
@@ -429,6 +429,11 @@
 free_data(struct gzip *gzip)
 {
 	if (gzip != NULL) {
+		/* Kernir patch 0013: a handle freed without close (state
+		 * FATAL, e.g. after archive_write_fail) never reached the
+		 * deflateEnd in close. deflateEnd is a no-op on a stream that
+		 * close ended or open never started (calloc'd). */
+		deflateEnd(&(gzip->stream));
 		free(gzip->compressed);
 		free(gzip->original_filename);
 		free(gzip);
--- a/libarchive/archive_write_add_filter_xz.c
+++ b/libarchive/archive_write_add_filter_xz.c
@@ -539,6 +539,11 @@
 free_data(struct xz *xz)
 {
 	if (xz != NULL) {
+		/* Kernir patch 0013: a handle freed without close (state
+		 * FATAL, e.g. after archive_write_fail) never reached the
+		 * lzma_end in close. lzma_end is a no-op on a stream that
+		 * close ended or open never started (calloc'd). */
+		lzma_end(&(xz->stream));
 		free(xz->compressed);
 		free(xz);
 	}
